ping. </ta><ta id="Seg_9539" s="T268" e="T269">What you / what the joke is that you uh ... </ta><ta id="Seg_9540" s="T269" e="T270">A solid on the dance floor , you can hit her . </ta><ta id="Seg_9541" s="T270" e="T272">You can tell her: "Watch out, you earn three hundred a night with us. </ta><ta id="Seg_9542" s="T272" e="T274">You're daft to be working as a shop assistant," for all I care. </ta><ta id="Seg_9543" s="T274" e="T278">" What you have there in a month , you can have there in a night . " . </ta><ta id="Seg_9544" s="T278" e="T281">And then I can bring it into the dormitory . </ta><ta id="Seg_9545" s="T281" e="T284">So the first f / uh , uh bringing her into the dormitory when she is not yet a Deerne, that is unpunishable . </ta><ta id="Seg_9546" s="T284" e="T285">That is reprehensible, but unpunishable . </ta><ta id="Seg_9547" s="T286" e="T287">Né ? </ta><ta id="Seg_9548" s="T287" e="T288">That's the joke. </ta><ta id="Seg_9549" s="T288" e="T291">You may / one who is already Deerne , you can not ankobern , but one who has not yet purchased , you may hit . </ta><ta id="Seg_9550" s="T291" e="T293">You can say: "Come on in. " . ˙</ta><ta id="Seg_9551" s="T296" e="T301">Well, most of the time, uh, uh, word gets around when they're on the goat. </ta><ta id="Seg_9552" s="T301" e="T302">And they have to go to the authorities twice a week, or some once. </ta><ta id="Seg_9553" s="T302" e="T307">And this one, she can / or she used to work there, in Herbertstrasse, has a friend there. </ta><ta id="Seg_9554" s="T307" e="T309">And she says: "Watch out, you can also move in with us. </ta><ta id="Seg_9555" s="T309" e="T312">You'll earn more with us . " . </ta><ta id="Seg_9556" s="T312" e="T314">Now there are better punters here than in Herbertstrasse or on the street at all , né ? </ta><ta id="Seg_9557" s="T314" e="T320">There they are also cobbling with twenty, sometimes with ten marks in ner Herbertstraße . </ta><ta id="Seg_9558" s="T320" e="T321">Or there are even five . </ta><ta id="Seg_9559" s="T321" e="T324">They're kobern for five marks . </ta><ta id="Seg_9560" s="T324" e="T326">And if you get a lot ... </ta><ta id="Seg_9561" s="T326" e="T327">you might get an average of thirty or thirty-five from the punter. </ta><ta id="Seg_9562" s="T327" e="T331">They also have compulsory drinks. </ta><ta id="Seg_9563" s="T331" e="T332">In a Herbertstraße . </ta><ta id="Seg_9564" s="T332" e="T334">That's not the case here . </ta><ta id="Seg_9565" s="T334" e="T337">They don't have to drink . </ta><ta id="Seg_9566" s="T339" e="T342">That depends on how long she works. </ta><ta id="Seg_9567" s="T342" e="T343">We have some who have an average of three, four or five hundred. </ta><ta id="Seg_9568" s="T343" e="T346">But others / well, just that they live from hand to mouth. </ta><ta id="Seg_9569" s="T346" e="T353">When they / if they have earned two hundred, then they stop and then they send it off. </ta><ta id="Seg_9570" s="T353" e="T355">And the next day they have no more marks on the seam, they don't save. </ta><ta id="Seg_9571" s="T355" e="T358">I don't even think that they put a few marks aside, save a bit and then / that they do something later, no? </ta><ta id="Seg_9572" s="T358" e="T361">There are others who have such grumpy lads. </ta><ta id="Seg_9573" s="T361" e="T364">They grab all the money and then drink it up, no? </ta><ta id="Seg_9574" s="T364" e="T366">That's very different, no? </ta><ta id="Seg_9575" s="T368" e="T369">It was a company of seven people . </ta><ta id="Seg_9576" s="T369" e="T372">And they were all from ... </ta><ta id="Seg_9577" s="T372" e="T373">So not from the catering trade or from Sankt Pauli, but very solid people who built it. </ta><ta id="Seg_9578" s="T373" e="T378">And after that, Bartels went in too.</ta><ta id="Seg_9579" s="T380" e="T382">Merchants . </ta><ta id="Seg_9580" s="T382" e="T385">And building contractors . </ta><ta id="Seg_9581" s="T385" e="T387">I don't even know / what they do in detail, I d